Account Management System

A terminal based user administration tool for Linux, built with bash and whiptail. It wraps common /etc/passwd, passwd, chage, usermod, and login-history commands behind a menu so you don't have to remember the raw syntax.

Installation

chmod +x account_mgmt.sh
sudo ./account_mgmt.sh

On first run the script creates a working folder at /tmp/AccountManagmentSys/ where it writes the text files it displays in scrollable dialogs.

Usage

Launch the script and use the arrow keys / number keys to pick a menu option, Enter to confirm, and Cancel/Esc to back out of a prompt. The main menu reappears after each action until you choose 0 or press Cancel from the main menu.

Output Files

Reports generated by options 1–5, 8, and 9 are written as plain text under:

Known Limitations

-No input validation on usernames/groups.
-Destructive actions have no confirmation step.
-Option 3 (password expiration) has a redirection issue.
-Inconsistent Cancel handling.

